  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["PR1", "H1", "C1"],
      "pins": ["PR1.VCC", "PR1.SDA", "PR1.SCL", "PR1.GND", "H1.1", "H1.2", "H1.3", "H1.4"],
      "nets": ["I2C_SDA", "I2C_SCL", "+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "In the 'Water Height Sensor' block the TF-Luna LiDAR symbol PR1 is drawn with solid wires (and a decoupling cap C1) connecting its VCC/SDA/SCL/GND pins through the 6-pin header H1 directly onto the +5V rail, GND, and the I2C_SDA / I2C_SCL nets. PR1 carries no DNP/no-connect marking, unlike the optional PR5/PR6 sensors which are crossed out.",
      "expected": "The specification states the LiDAR is intentionally excluded from this build: 'its pins are \"free\" and it is marked on_board: no / excluded from the board; it is not wired into any net' and 'all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design.' The wired water-level interface is the ultrasonic scheme, not a LiDAR on the I2C bus.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "§4.3 ... the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no, in_bom: yes, and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "§6 Known Limitations ... TF-Luna LiDAR is unwired ... its pins are typed free, it is marked on_board: no, and it has no corresponding firmware code."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1, 'Water Height Sensor': PR1 LIDAR pins VCC/SDA/SCL/GND wired to H1, which is connected to +5V, GND, I2C_SDA and I2C_SCL (no no-connect markers, no DNP cross)."}
      ],
      "impact": "A 5 V I2C rangefinder that the design deliberately leaves unconnected is now bridged onto the 3.3 V main I2C bus (with 2.2 k pull-ups). This loads/level-conflicts the bus, can introduce an address collision, and changes the water-level sensing path from the intended ultrasonic GPIO scheme to an unexpected LiDAR, so the board behaves differently from the reference design.",
      "confidence": 0.68
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing deviates from the intended design by wiring the TF-Luna LiDAR (PR1) onto the +5V/GND/I2C bus via H1, whereas the specification repeatedly states PR1 is excluded (on_board: no, pins free, not connected to any net); this is the only clear anomaly found."
}

